---
description: Extract Check Point fields from a read_syslog message field
---

// `parse_kv` infers a type per value, so a Check Point field whose text looks
// like a number or an address arrives as an `int64` or an `ip` rather than a
// string — a numeric login name, an `sname` that is a bare address. The OCSF
// mappers coerce those back, because `ocsf::cast` drops a mistyped value
// rather than converting it. The JSON export path is unaffected, since JSON
// states the type.
this = {
  ...message.parse_kv(field_split="\\|", value_split="="),
  syslog: {
    facility: move facility?,
    severity: move severity?,
    version: move version?,
    timestamp: move timestamp?,
    hostname: move hostname?,
    app_name: move app_name?,
    process_id: move process_id?,
    message_id: move message_id?,
  },
}

checkpoint::parse
